To control token usage, the tutor is designed so that most interactions do not use the LLM.
Professor-approved questions, hints, solution steps, and misconceptions are stored in the database and served directly.
The LLM is used only as a fallback when the stored material is not enough.
The production path enforces per-student/question and per-session limits, an optional daily allowance, a burst limit, input length limits, short AI responses, caching, and durable usage accounting.
This prevents students from freely consuming unlimited tokens while still giving them useful tutoring support.
